{
  "title": "Goldenhar Syndrome",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/12745/goldenhar-syndrome",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 16 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Goldenhar Syndrome, also known as oculo-auriculo-vertebral spectrum, is a rare congenital disorder caused by an error in the embryological development of the ectoderm, that presents with thoracic scoliosis, crainofacial microsomia, and ocular desmoid cysts.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made based on family history associated with typical clinical features.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment involves a multidisciplinary approach to address spine manifestations, ocular abnormalities, and craniofascial abnormalities.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "relatively rare",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "seen in 1:3500-25000 births",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "affects males more than females (3:2)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "results from an **error in the embryological development of the ectoderm**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "leads to unilateral arrest or dysplastic development of",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "first and second branchial arches",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "first pharyngeal pouch",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "branchial cleft",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inheritance",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "multifactorial but usually sporadic",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may have a genetic component",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "rarely inherited in an autosomal dominant pattern (1-2%)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**spine**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "thoracic scoliosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "defects of vertebral segmentation (cervical most common)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**face**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12745/images/screen_shot_2017-01-14_at_3.51.22_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "partially formed or absent ear (microtia)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "benign growths around the eye (ocular desmoid cysts)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12745/images/goldenhar_syndrome_limbal_dermoid.jpg",
                      "caption": "ocular lesions"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "chin or mouth deviated to the affected side",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/12745/images/goldenhar_syndrome.jpg",
                      "caption": "facial asymmetry"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "cleft lip/palate",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**systemic**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "hearing defects",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "kidney defects",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "normal intelligence",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
